# Architecture and Layering

- **Layers and responsibilities**
  - Use the existing projects strictly:
    - `*.Domain.Shared`: base entities, shared abstractions, exceptions, extensions, per-entity consts.
    - `*.Domain`: domain entities and domain-specific repository interfaces only.
    - `*.Application.Contracts`: DTOs and application service interfaces, no business logic.
    - `*.Application`: application services, background jobs, AutoMapper profiles, no direct `DbContext`.
    - `*.EntityFrameworkCore`: `ApplicationDbContext`, entity configurations, repository implementations.
    - `*.HttpApi`: controllers, HTTP attributes, filters.
    - `*.HttpApi.Host`: host, middlewares, logging, configuration.

- **Vertical slice per entity/module**
  - When adding a new entity/module (e.g. `Todo`), mirror the existing `User`/`Role` pattern:
    - Domain.Shared: `{Entity}Consts` in `{EntityName}/` folder.
    - Domain: `{Entity}` entity in `{EntityName}/` folder.
    - Application.Contracts: request/response DTOs and `I{Entity}AppService`.
    - Application: `{Entity}AppService` implementation.
    - EntityFrameworkCore: `{Entity}Configuration` and `{Entity}Repository`.
    - HttpApi: `{Entity}Controller` with v1 route.

- **Naming conventions (summary)**
  - Entities: `{Entity}` in `*.Domain/{EntityName}/{EntityName}.cs`.
  - DTOs: `{Action}{Entity}RequestDto`, `{Entity}ResponseDto` in `*.Application.Contracts/{EntityName}/`.
  - App services: `I{Entity}AppService` / `{Entity}AppService` under the corresponding contracts/application folders.
  - Repositories: `I{Entity}Repository` in `*.Domain/Repositories/`, `{Entity}Repository` in `*.EntityFrameworkCore/Repositories/`.
  - Controllers: `{Entity}Controller` in `*.HttpApi/Controllers/v1/`.
  - EF configurations: `{Entity}Configuration` in `*.EntityFrameworkCore/EntityConfigurations/`.

- **General technical rules**
  - All data access goes through repositories; services should not depend on `ApplicationDbContext`.
  - All controller responses use DTOs; never expose domain entities directly over HTTP.
  - Prefer async everywhere, always take `CancellationToken cancellationToken = default`.
  - Use project-specific exception types (`AppValidationException`, `AppEntityNotFoundException`, etc.) with localized messages.

